To define the degrees of freedom for the shape function space $P_k(K; \mathbb{S})$, let $  x_0, \cdots,   x_n$ be the vertices of simplex $K$. The referencing mapping is then \a{   x: &= F_K(\hat {  x}) =   x_0 + \p{   x_1 -  x_0, & \cdots,&   x_n -  x_0 } \hat{  x}, } mapping the reference tetrahedron $\hat K:=\{ 0 \le \hat x_1, \cdots, \hat x_n, 1-\sum\limits_{i=1}^n\hat x_i \le 1 \}$ to $K$. Then the inverse mapping is \an{ \lab{imap} \hat {  x}: &= \p{  
u_1^T\ \vdots \   
u_n^T} (  x-  x_0), } where \an{\lab{nnt} \p{  
u_1^T\ \vdots \   
u_n^T }=\p{   x_1 -  x_0, & \cdots, &   x_n -  x_0}^{-1}. } By \meqref{imap}, these normal vectors are coefficients of the barycentric variables: \a{ \lambda_1: &=   
u_1 \cdot (  x-  x_0), \ \vdots & \ \lambda_n: &=   
u_n \cdot (  x-  x_0), \ \lambda_0: &= 1-\sum\limits_{i=1}^n\lambda_i. }
